# Claude Code — memory scopes, ratified in docs/decisions/0004-ctxpack-memory-scopes.md.
#
# LOCAL by default: raw CtxPack session records, gists and the checkpoint ledger
# are operational memory. They carry machine-specific absolute paths, verbatim
# user prompts and cross-repository working context, so publishing them in a
# release archive publishes the operator, not the product (#39). They stay on
# disk and out of the tree — nothing here deletes an owner's ledger.
#
# PUBLIC is opt-in and explicit: only .claude/ctx/public/ is tracked, and only a
# sanitized projection belongs there. A new raw session cannot reach a release by
# default, which is the property the previous `!.claude/ctx/` blanket un-ignore
# did not have.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/ctx/
.claude/ctx/*
!.claude/ctx/public/

# Temp
*.tmp
*.bak

# Internal working docs — local-only, never published
docs/internal/
docs/deliverables/
docs/plans/
